          "filename": "Levens Hall from The Main Gates - geograph.org.uk - 1399553.jpg",
          "caption": "Levens Hall from The Main Gates Levens Hall is a magnificent Elizabethan House built around a 13th century Pele Tower and Great Hall.  This early fortified building was enlarged and refurbished in the 16th century by James Bellingham who used wood panelling, leather wall coverings, tapestries and plasterwork to enhance his surroundings.  When his kinsman, Colonel James Grahme inherited the house, he added servants' quarters kitchens and a brewhouse.",
          "alt": "Levens Hall from The Main Gates Levens Hall is a magnificent Elizabethan House built around a 13th century Pele Tower and Great Hall.  This early fortified building was enlarged and refurbished in the 16th century by James Bellingham who used wood panelling, leather wall coverings, tapestries and plasterwork to enhance his surroundings.  When his kinsman, Colonel James Grahme inherited the house, he added servants' quarters kitchens and a brewhouse.",
